        "original_id": "ac23c1b1-d149-5107-a68f-0d6c5274aa7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Oliver Bierhoff, Thomas Helveg, Alberto Zaccheroni\n- Organizations: Udinese Calcio, Milan, Germany national football team\n- Events: 1998–99 Udinese Calcio season, UEFA Euro 1996 Final\n- Roles: Topscorer, midfielder, coach, footballer\n\nFacts:\n- On 1 May 1968, Oliver Bierhoff was born.\n- In the UEFA Euro 1996 Final, Oliver Bierhoff scored the first golden goal in major international football for the Germany national football team.\n- Oliver Bierhoff is a retired German former footballer.\n- Before the start of the 1998–99 Udinese Calcio season, Udinese Calcio appeared to be at a disadvantage because topscorer Oliver Bierhoff, midfielder Thomas Helveg, and coach Alberto Zaccheroni all left for Milan.",
